  "notes": "Verified 2026-09-17 by fetching the real archived 2024-25 bulletin page directly (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/.../aerospace-engineering-bs/). Confirmed identical to the 2022-23 and 2023-24 editions (AERSP-2022.json / AERSP-2023.json): same 131-credit total (General Education 45 credits, 27 of which are embedded in the major, Requirements for the Major 113-117 credits), same 8-semester sequence and per-semester credit subtotals (15/17/16/16/16.5/17/16.5/17), same Design Sequence choice (AERSP 401A/401B or 402A/402B paired with 413/450), and the same 6+3+3 Aerospace/General Technical/Limited elective split. 'Prerequisites Before Junior Year' language (EMCH 212, the CMPSC programming requirement, MATH 220, MATH 230, MATH 250/251) matches AERSP-2026.json's own sequencing exactly -- nothing in this year's flowchart needed reordering. As with 2022-23/2023-24, ME 201 is the only thermal-science course named in the bulletin (no ME 300 substitute -- that comes from the department's current, undated curriculum guide PDF with no archived per-year equivalent), and the First-Year Seminar requirement is stated generically, so AERSP-2026.json's widened 13-code FYS option list and 2-option ECON 102/104 item (matching its own pre-existing ECON 14 gap) are both carried forward unchanged. Elective wiring and the MATH 21 CHEM 110 prereq-chain fallback are likewise carried forward unchanged for the same catalog-not-year-scoped reasons documented in AERSP-2022.json.",
